#: kcmlayout.cpp:91
msgid "&Enable keyboard layouts"
msgstr "&Cho phe'p kie^?u ba`n phi'm"

#: kcmlayout.cpp:92
msgid ""
"Here you can completely disable this module, for example if you use other "
"tools for switching keyboard layouts."
msgstr ""
"Ba.n co' the^? hoa`n toa`n kho^ng du`ng module na`y , vi' du. ne'u ba.n du`ng"
"ca'c co^ng cu. kha'c dde^? thay ddo^?i kie^?u ba`n phi'm ."

#: kcmlayout.cpp:117
msgid "Keyboard &Model:"
msgstr "&Kie^?u ba`n phi'm :"

#: kcmlayout.cpp:120
msgid ""
"Here you can choose a keyboard model. This setting is independent of your "
"keyboard layout and refers to the \"hardware\" model, i.e. the way your "
"keyboard is manufactured. Modern keyboards that come with your computer "
"usually have two extra keys and are referred to as \"104-key\" models, which "
"is probably what you want if you don't know what kind of keyboard you have."
msgstr ""
"Ba.n co' the^? cho.n kie^?u ba.n phi'm o+? dda^y . Ca'c thie^'t la^.p na`y ddo^.c la^.p "
"vo+'i kie^?u ba`n phi'm va` ddo^.c la^.p vo+'i kie^?u \"pha^`n cu+'ng\" ddu+o+.c"
"dde^` ca^.p , nghi~a la` ca'ch ma` ba`n phi'm cu?a ba.n ddu+o+.c che^' ta.o ."
"Kie^?u ba`n phi'm ddi cu`ng vo+'i ma'y ti'nh cu?a ba.n thu+o+`ng co' the^m 2 phi'm ddu+o+.c"
"dde^` ca^.p dde^'n nhu+ la` kie^?u \"104 phi'm\2 . Loa.i na`y thu+o+`ng ddu+o+.c"
"du`ng ne^'u ba.n kho^ng bie^'t kie^?u ba`n phi'm ma` ba.n ddang du`ng la` loa.i gi` ."

#: kcmlayout.cpp:130
msgid "Primary L&ayout:"
msgstr "&Kie^?u ba`n phi'm chi'nh :"

#: kcmlayout.cpp:133
msgid ""
"Here you can choose your primary keyboard layout, i.e. the keyboard layout "
"used as default. The keyboard layout defines \"which keys do what\". For "
"example German keyboards have the letter 'Y' where US keyboards have the "
"letter 'Z'."
msgstr ""
"Ba.n co' the^? cho.n kie^`u ba`n phi'm chi'nh o+? dda^y, nghi~a la` kie^?u ba`n phi'm"
"se~ ddu+o+.c du`ng ma(.c ddi.nh . Kie^?u ba`n phi'm ddi.nh nghi~a \"phi'm na`o"
"la`m ca'i gi`\" . Vi' du., ba`n phi'm DDu+'c co' chu+~ 'Y' trong khi ba`n phi'm US"
"co' phi'm 'Z' ."

#: kcmlayout.cpp:143
msgid "&Primary Variant:"
msgstr "Bie^'n the^? &chi'nh :"

#: kcmlayout.cpp:146
msgid ""
"Here you can choose a variant of your primary keyboard layout. Layout "
"variants usually represent different key maps for the same language. For "
"example, Ukrainian layout might have four variants: basic, winkeys (as in "
"Windows), typewriter (as in typewriters) and phonetic (each Ukrainian letter "
"is placed on a transliterated latin one)."
msgstr ""
"Ba.n co' the^? cho.n bie^'n the^? cu?a ba`n phi'm chi'nh  . Kie^?u bie^'n the^?"
"thu+o+`ng the^? hie^.n key map kha'c cho cu`ng mo^.t ngo^n ngu+~ . Vi' du. ,"
"ba`n phi'm ukraina thu+o+'ng co' 4 bie^'n the^? : co+ ba?n, winkey ( nhu+ Windows),"
"dda'nh ma'y ( nhu+ la` dda'nh ma'y) va` phonetic ."

#: kcmlayout.cpp:157
msgid "Additional layouts"
msgstr "Ca'c kie^?u phu."

#: kcmlayout.cpp:161
msgid ""
"You can select an arbitrary number of additional keyboard layouts. If one or "
"more additional layouts have been selected, the KDE panel will offer a "
"docked flag. By clicking on this flag you can easily switch between layouts."
msgstr ""
"Ba.n co' the^? cho.n mo^.t so^' ba^'t i` ca'c kie^?u ba`n phi'm phu. . Ne^'u mo^.t"
"hay nhie^`u kie^?u phu. ddu+o+.c cho.n, khung KDE se~ cung ca^'p mo^.t  la' co+' ."
"Ba(`ng vie^.c nha^'n va`o la' co+` na`y, ba.n co' the^? de^ ~da`ng chuye^?n"
"giu+~a ca'c ba`n phi'm ."

#: kcmlayout.cpp:172
msgid "Flag"
msgstr "La' co+`"

#: kcmlayout.cpp:173
msgid "Layout"
msgstr "Kie^?u"

#: kcmlayout.cpp:174
msgid "Keymap"
msgstr "Keymap"

#: kcmlayout.cpp:185
msgid "&Variant:"
msgstr "&Bie^'n the^?"

#: kcmlayout.cpp:189
msgid ""
"Here you can choose a variant of the selected additional keyboard layout. "
"Layout variants usually represent different key maps for the same language. "
"For example, Ukrainian layout might have four variants: basic, winkeys (as "
"in Windows), typewriter (as in typewriters) and phonetic (each Ukrainian "
"letter is placed on a transliterated latin one)."
msgstr ""
"Ba.n co' the^? cho. 1 bie^'n the^? cu?a ca'c kie^?u ba`n phi'm phu. ."
"Kie^?u bie^'n the^? the^? hie^.n mo^.t keymap kha'c cu?a cu`ng mo^.t ngo^n ngu+~ ."
"Vi' du., Kie^?u ukraina co' bo^'n kie^?u : co+ ba?n, dda'nh ma'y, winkeys va` phonetic"

