#: kcmmisc.cpp:49
msgid "&Keyboard repeat"
msgstr "La(.p &ba`n phi'm"

#: kcmmisc.cpp:53
msgid ""
"If you check this option, pressing and holding down a key emits the same "
"character over and over again. For example, pressing and holding down the "
"Tab key will have the same effect as that of pressing that key several times "
"in succession: Tab characters continue to be emitted until you release the "
"key."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u ba.n nha^.n tuy` cho.n na`y, nha^'n va` giu+~ mo^.t phi'm se~ kho^ng la`m"
"la(.p nhie^`u la^`n . Vi' du., nha^`n va` giu+~ phi'm Tab se~ kho^ng la`m cho no' co'"
"nghi~a la` nha^'n phi'm tab nhie^`u la^`n : Phi'm tab chi? co' y' nghi~a tro+? la.i"
" sau khi ba.n nha? no' ra ."

#: kcmmisc.cpp:62
msgid "Key click &volume:"
msgstr "A^m &thanh nha^'n phi'm :"

#: kcmmisc.cpp:70
msgid ""
"If supported, this option allows you to hear audible clicks from your "
"computer's speakers when you press the keys on your keyboard. This might be "
"useful if your keyboard does not have mechanical keys, or if the sound that "
"the keys make is very soft.<p> You can change the loudness of the key click "
"feedback by dragging the slider button or by clicking the up/down arrows on "
"the spin-button. Setting the volume to 0 % turns off the key click."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u ddu+o+.c ho^~ tro+., tuy` cho.n na`y se~ cho phe'p ba.n nghe tie^'ng click"
"tu+` loa cu?a ma'y ti'nh khi ba.n nha^'n va`o ba`n phi'm . No' co' the^? se~"
"ra^'t co' i'ch ne^'u ma'y ti'nh cu?a ba.n kho^ng co' ca'c phi'm co+ ho.c , hay tie^'ng"
"nha^'n phi'm qua' nho? . <p> Ba.n co' the^? thay ddo^?i ddo^. lo+'n cu?a a^m"
"thanh ba(`ng ca'ch ke'o tha? va`o thanh tru+o+.c hay du`ng mu~i te^n le^n xuo^'ng ."
"DDa(.t a^m thanh la` 0 % dde^? ta('t ."

#: kcmmisc.cpp:81
